    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0488" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg390"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 283.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                        applications<anchor n="1" xml:id="d513-f1"/> for passport of Logan Herbert
                    Roots and Oliver Tracey Logan, which I have declined to issue on the ground that
                    it would be contrary to the instructions and regulations of the State Department
                    governing the issuance of passports, since in each case the applicant has no
                    intention of returning to the United States, and so expressly states in his
                    application.</p>
                <p>I also inclose copies of correspondence with the United States consul at Hankau
                    on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>






